2): Overkill with such a weak hand. Only justifiable as a deep bluff, but extremely exploitable and low-EV here.\n\nBest Move: Fold.  \nOur hand is the worst possible starting hand in terms of raw strength. It has no high card value, no pair potential, no straight or flush prospects beyond extreme longshots. We are out of position, and the opponent has shown strength by raising. Calling or raising turns this into a pure bluff or luck draw, which isn’t sustainable.\n\nWe are in the chip lead overall — optimal strategy now favors conservatism to preserve edge. No need to gamble unnecessarily.\n\nReason:  \nFolding preserves chips and avoids marginal spots with a hand that has negligible equity against any reasonable opening range. Our position, lack of connectivity, and poor rank make calling or raising -EV.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
